                        ],
                        "form": "приключи́вшийся"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b9c3e379-65cd-468e-9a18-c2b747f7c657",
                        "entry_id": "6d127969-62e3-3c49-a1a6-cf25edd1044a",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "приключи́вшись"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0fbeaae4-b61c-37f6-bc49-a67d94d599c2",
                        "entry_id": "6d127969-62e3-3c49-a1a6-cf25edd1044a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. то же, что случиться"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "37dec2cf-6ce9-4d95-aa1d-fe50ef1cfd8a",
                                "sense_id": "0fbeaae4-b61c-37f6-bc49-a67d94d599c2",
                                "text": "Учтивый приятель мой уверял госпожу NN, что ему не приключилось в самом деле никакого вреда, кроме испуга."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d3e6c31-71d6-47eb-87f4-07dede91577e",
                                "sense_id": "0fbeaae4-b61c-37f6-bc49-a67d94d599c2",
                                "text": "― Каким же образом, какими судьбами это приключилось?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9bcfe2e7-1b94-4371-825f-5340cb5c6d1f",
                                "sense_id": "0fbeaae4-b61c-37f6-bc49-a67d94d599c2",
                                "text": "Катерина Савишна уверяет, что с тобой удар приключился."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ee49cc3a-34e8-4530-9532-93163455cb4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d127969-62e3-3c49-a1a6-cf25edd1044a",
                        "source_sense_id": "0fbeaae4-b61c-37f6-bc49-a67d94d599c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "happen",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "happen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a7f5833-f9f5-36a8-adfe-d65b6b64c59e",
                                        "entry_id": "af6c917e-9853-3f12-a087-21f6c90f0817",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To occur or take place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ce40fb0-4caa-4785-b5ea-f6e9719e0ed2",
                                                "sense_id": "7a7f5833-f9f5-36a8-adfe-d65b6b64c59e",
                                                "text": "Let me tell you how it happened."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b8f6daa-d395-4518-9ff0-5fdf069e1d73",
                                                "sense_id": "7a7f5833-f9f5-36a8-adfe-d65b6b64c59e",
                                                "text": "Seeing the British establishment struggle with the financial sector is like watching an alcoholic who still resists the idea that something drastic needs to happen for him to turn his life around."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30f3722f-4d0f-3327-bff8-02d7ac1fea73",
                                        "entry_id": "af6c917e-9853-3f12-a087-21f6c90f0817",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To happen to; to befall."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2bbddb9-9414-48c5-a6d1-1ed052427b80",
                                                "sense_id": "30f3722f-4d0f-3327-bff8-02d7ac1fea73",
                                                "text": "'By my soul! I believe something bad has happened me,' he muttered, and popped up his window, and looked out, half dreaming over the church-yard on the park beyond […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "004d385d-4014-3747-b223-d85790ff954d",
                                        "entry_id": "af6c917e-9853-3f12-a087-21f6c90f0817",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To do or occur by chance or unexpectedly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "impersonal",
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "with-infinitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f20cbb6-5d5a-44c4-8034-3e7781f70975",
                                                "sense_id": "004d385d-4014-3747-b223-d85790ff954d",
                                                "text": "Take an umbrella in case it happens to rain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bba5552-ad3d-4023-80f9-b152bb0c4281",
                                                "sense_id": "004d385d-4014-3747-b223-d85790ff954d",
                                                "text": "Do you happen to have an umbrella?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02637478-3d08-4829-aa80-030eca49d44d",
                                                "sense_id": "004d385d-4014-3747-b223-d85790ff954d",
                                                "text": "If you should (happen to) need any help, I'll be there."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aca9ba2e-986b-34f1-a1b5-afabd511332f",
                                        "entry_id": "af6c917e-9853-3f12-a087-21f6c90f0817",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To encounter by chance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "followed by on or upon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef7e44cf-51d2-4e43-b2a6-f3876c4bb898",
                                                "sense_id": "aca9ba2e-986b-34f1-a1b5-afabd511332f",
                                                "text": "Unexpectedly, in a nook close by the farmhouse, he happened upon a spot where the vintage had actually commenced."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cdc59d8-e6e7-310c-a02d-281bea99f0cd",
                                        "entry_id": "af6c917e-9853-3f12-a087-21f6c90f0817",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become popular or trendy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "happen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65251ee1-625d-300c-a3bb-b59bb43dd6cb",
                                        "entry_id": "98f5886e-fa5f-389d-848f-2a02cc4afa1f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "maybe, perhaps."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal",
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61ceb884-6e5a-4da7-9614-56688b22ff08",
                                                "sense_id": "65251ee1-625d-300c-a3bb-b59bb43dd6cb",
                                                "text": "Yeah, well happen if he'd gone quietly, she wouldn't have needed to show him who's in charge."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a5e515a7-b72d-48c9-a4a3-efe023761502",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d127969-62e3-3c49-a1a6-cf25edd1044a",
                        "source_sense_id": "0fbeaae4-b61c-37f6-bc49-a67d94d599c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "occur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "occur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e15040b-d1d1-357c-9680-f97f66bb8159",
                                        "entry_id": "11b79b9e-c6ab-3228-902e-b5acf2e07dec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To happen or take place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65046314-96f2-4a97-812b-51a42faa19c8",
                                                "sense_id": "5e15040b-d1d1-357c-9680-f97f66bb8159",
                                                "text": "The liftoff will occur in exactly twelve seconds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fb6ac38-a732-45d4-ba1c-4e7de994f769",
                                                "sense_id": "5e15040b-d1d1-357c-9680-f97f66bb8159",
                                                "text": "And no use for anyone to tell Charles that this was because the Family was in mourning for Mr Granville Darracott […]: Charles might only have been second footman at Darracott Place for a couple of months when that disaster occurred, but no one could gammon him into thinking that my lord cared a spangle for his heir."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab156b78-3712-36cb-96ca-e40e8af56a36",
